      "title": "An added benefit has its own qualifying event",
      "narration": "Elena compares four optional features on a life policy. One adds money after a qualifying accidental death. Another preserves opportunities to purchase more protection even if health changes. A third adjusts coverage using an inflation measure. A fourth adds a death benefit linked to premiums under its formula. These features solve different problems. The word rider does not mean every feature pays cash immediately or lasts as long as the base policy. Identify the covered event, the amount, the election conditions and the ending provisions. Then read the cost. A familiar feature name is a starting point, not a substitute for the actual contract.",
