      "title": "Accidental death does not always mean double",
      "narration": "Assume a covered two hundred thousand dollar base death benefit and a fifty thousand dollar accidental-death rider. If the death meets both provisions and no adjustment applies, the total is two hundred fifty thousand dollars. It is not automatically four hundred thousand. Double indemnity describes a design that adds an amount equal to the base benefit; other designs add different amounts. Read whether the accident caused the death, the required time between injury and death, exclusions and the rider's ending age. If a death qualifies under the base policy but not the accident rider, the base benefit may still be payable under its own terms.",
