      "title": "Solve the event before choosing the feature",
      "narration": "Now Elena asks which feature addresses concern about becoming difficult to insure later. A defined guaranteed-insurability opportunity directly addresses that concern. An accidental-death benefit addresses a different cause-of-death condition. An inflation rider addresses the stated change in coverage. The final rider adds a death benefit based on eligible premiums under its formula. On an exam, underline the event and the requested result. Then calculate only the amounts that the facts trigger. Check whether the option must be elected and whether a deadline, exclusion or coverage limit changes the answer. That approach connects the rider's purpose to the actual case instead of choosing the most attractive sounding feature.",
